        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Mooreville, Mississippi; Dorsey; Tupelo; Byhalia; Memphis, Tennessee; Birmingham, Alabama; Hollywood, California\n- Roads: Mississippi Highway 178; Interstate 22; U.S. Route 78\n- People: Olin Caldwell Francis\n- Topics: location and biography\n\nFacts:\n- Olin Caldwell Francis was born on September 13, 1891 in Mooreville, Mississippi.\n- Olin Caldwell Francis was known for \"A Knight of the West\" (1921), \"Fightin' Devil\" (1922), and \"The Kid Brother\" (1927).\n- Interstate 22 is an Interstate Highway that follows the U.S. Route 78 corridor for 213 miles from Byhalia, Mississippi, south of Memphis, Tennessee, to Birmingham, Alabama.\n- Olin Caldwell Francis died on June 30, 1952 in Hollywood, California.\n- Mooreville, Mississippi is approximately 4 miles west of Dorsey and approximately 4 miles east of Tupelo on Mississippi Highway 178 near Interstate 22.",
